cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "KinectTUG-Gait: Instrumented Timed-Up-and-Go gait analysis from Kinect v2 skeletal data"
abstract: >-
  A MATLAB toolbox that reproduces the gait-processing pipeline described in the
  accompanying manuscript: load Kinect v2 skeleton tracking (25 joints), denoise
  with a zero-phase 4th-order Butterworth low-pass (5 Hz, 30 fps), transform to a
  subject-centred frame via PCA of the centre-of-mass displacement, automatically
  segment the Timed-Up-and-Go (TUG) test into stand-up / walk / turn / sit-down,
  detect gait events (heel-strike / toe-off) from the ankle forward (depth) trajectory,
  and extract spatiotemporal gait parameters from a single representative
  cycle (the "6-point method").
